					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-866463#post-2108261</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-866463/scp-002-j#post-2108261</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 12 Sep 2014 10:46:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>VAElynx</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>914331</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Upvoted because the concept just occured to me and I'm vaguely glad someone saved me the time.</span></p> <p>Nah, it's genuinely funny. I just think the punchline could be better. An old-time log from the time the Foundation still used them. Imagine this - two people come visit you under a flimsy pretext that soon falls as they ask you more and more questions Men-in-Black style&#8230;. and once they are done, they leave a confused amnesiac with you in the house and leave, content that they have maintained secrecy.<br /> Doubly so if the person visited is the creator of some anomalous works.<br /> Triply so if the amnesiac <em>works</em>, perhaps by upsetting the person's concentration enough to carry on with their work.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
